{"cuisine/lahori-cuisine":{"t":"cuisine","r":"cuisine/lahori-cuisine","n":"Lahori cuisine","c":"#f0b340","crumb":[["Asia","cuisines#asia"],["Punjabi cuisine","cuisine/punjabi-cuisine"]],"sub":"Regional cuisine in India","intro":[["Lahori cuisine refers to the food and cuisine of the city of Lahore in Punjab, Pakistan. It is a part of regional Punjabi cuisine. Lahore is a city with an extremely rich food culture.  People from Lahore are famous all over the country for their love for food. The city offers a vast variety of options when it comes to gastronomy. In recent times, the style of food has achieved popularity in a  number of different countries, because of its palatable and milder taste,  mainly through the Pakistani diaspora."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"lahori-cuisine"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lahori_cuisine"}],"sections":[{"h":"Recipe sites","empty":"None yet","tryLinks":[["Punjabi cuisine","cuisine/punjabi-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Part of","links":[["Punjabi cuisine","cuisine/punjabi-cuisine"]]}],"cont":"Asian cuisine","img":{"src":"/labs/cuisines/img/thumb/c/c4/Pakistani_Food_Karahi_Beef.jpg/500px-Pakistani_Food_Karahi_Beef.jpg","w":500,"h":335,"by":"Jess Lander from Culver City, CA, USA","lic":"CC BY 2.0","licUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/2.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Pakistani_Food_Karahi_Beef.jpg"}},"cuisine/franconian-cuisine":{"t":"cuisine","r":"cuisine/franconian-cuisine","n":"Franconian cuisine","c":"#cf5f87","crumb":[["Europe","cuisines#europe"],["German cuisine","cuisine/german-cuisine"]],"sub":"Regional cuisine in Germany","intro":[["Franconian cuisine is an umbrella term for all dishes that nominally belong to the region of Franconia. It is a subtype of German cuisine with many similarities to Bavarian cuisine and Swabian cuisine. It is often included in the Bavarian cuisine, since most parts of Franconia belong to Bavaria today. There are several Franconian food items that are also famous beyond the borders of Franconia, such as Nürnberger Lebkuchen, Bratwurst and the wines of Franconia. Franconia is also famous for its beer and harbours the highest density of breweries in the world."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"franconian-cuisine"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Franconian_cuisine"}],"sections":[{"h":"Recipe sites","count":1,"rows":[{"name":"Nuremberg Tourism: Franconian specialties","ref":"site/tourismus-nuernberg-de","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"tourismus.nuernberg.de","note":"Nuremberg's official tourism site, with a section of Franconian specialty recipes such as Schäufele.","url":"https://tourismus.nuernberg.de/en/food-drink/nurembergs-specialties/franconian-specialties/recipe-franconian-schaeuferle-pork-shoulder-in-beer-sauce-1/","suggested":true}]},{"h":"Part of","links":[["German cuisine","cuisine/german-cuisine"]]}],"cont":"European cuisine","img":{"src":"/labs/cuisines/img/thumb/b/b1/Sch%C3%A4ufele.JPG/500px-Sch%C3%A4ufele.JPG","w":500,"h":352,"by":"User: Benreis at wikivoyage shared","lic":"CC BY-SA 3.0","licUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Sch%C3%A4ufele.JPG"}},"cuisine/cuisine-of-the-ionian-islands":{"t":"cuisine","r":"cuisine/cuisine-of-the-ionian-islands","n":"Cuisine of the Ionian Islands","c":"#cf5f87","crumb":[["Europe","cuisines#europe"],["Greek cuisine","cuisine/greek-cuisine"]],"sub":"Regional cuisine in Greece","intro":[["The Cuisine of the Ionian islands or Heptanesean cuisine is a type of Greek cuisine associated with the Ionian Islands region. It has more influences from Italian cuisine than can be found in any other part of Greece due to the long period of Venetian rule in the Ionian Islands."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"cuisine-of-the-ionian-islands"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cuisine_of_the_Ionian_Islands"}],"sections":[{"h":"Recipe sites","count":1,"rows":[{"name":"Greek Recipe: Corfu","ref":"site/greek-recipe-com","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"greek-recipe.com","note":"Regional category of Corfiot dishes such as pastitsada on a Greek recipe site.","url":"https://greek-recipe.com/category/regional/corfu","suggested":true}]},{"h":"Part of","links":[["Greek cuisine","cuisine/greek-cuisine"]]}],"cont":"European cuisine"},"cuisine/vanuatuan-cuisine":{"t":"cuisine","r":"cuisine/vanuatuan-cuisine","n":"Vanuatuan cuisine","c":"#55b8ad","crumb":[["Oceania","cuisines#oceania"],["Cuisine"]],"sub":"National cuisine of Vanuatu","intro":[["The cuisine of Vanuatu incorporates fish, root vegetables such as taro and yams, fruits, and vegetables. Most island families grow food in their gardens, and food shortages are rare. Papayas, pineapples, mangoes, plantains, and sweet potatoes are abundant through much of the year. Coconut milk and coconut cream are used to flavour many dishes. Most food is cooked using hot stones or through boiling and steaming; little food is fried. Since Vanuatu is one of the few South Pacific regions influenced by the outside world, Vanuatu's food has a multicultural nature."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"vanuatuan-cuisine"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vanuatuan_cuisine"}],"sections":[{"h":"Recipe sites","empty":"None yet","tryLinks":[]},{"h":"Cookbooks","count":2,"rows":[{"name":"Me'a Kai: The Food and Flavours of the South Pacific","ref":"cookbook/me-a-kai-the-food-and-flavours-of-the-south-pacific","color":"#f0b340","shape":"book","sub":"Robert Oliver, Tracy Berno and Shiri Ram, 2010","note":"Regional cookbook with a chapter on Vanuatu.","url":"https://openlibrary.org/books/OL28452199M","suggested":true},{"name":"Eat Pacific: The Pacific Island Food Revolution Cookbook","ref":"cookbook/eat-pacific-the-pacific-island-food-revolution-cookbook","color":"#f0b340","shape":"book","sub":"Robert Oliver (ed.), 2024","note":"Pacific Island Food Revolution cookbook with a Vanuatu section.","url":"https://masseypress.ac.nz/books/eat-pacific","suggested":true}]}],"cont":"Oceanic cuisine","img":{"src":"/labs/cuisines/img/thumb/8/85/Vanuatu_Beef_Curry_with_Boiled_Taro.jpg/500px-Vanuatu_Beef_Curry_with_Boiled_Taro.jpg","w":500,"h":376,"by":"Asamboi","lic":"CC BY-SA 4.0","licUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Vanuatu_Beef_Curry_with_Boiled_Taro.jpg"}},"dish/bergh-stoutenburgh-house":{"t":"dish","r":"dish/bergh-stoutenburgh-house","n":"Bergh–Stoutenburgh House","c":"#ede6da","crumb":[["Dishes","dishes"]],"sub":"Dish from Japanese cuisine","dot":"#f0b340","intro":[["The Bergh–Stoutenburgh House is located on U.S. Route 9 opposite Mansion Drive in Hyde Park, New York. It is currently used as a district office by state senator Sue Serino."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-bergh-stoutenburgh-house"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bergh%E2%80%93Stoutenburgh_House"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["Japanese cuisine","cuisine/japanese-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Cook it","rows":[{"name":"Just One Cookbook","ref":"site/justonecookbook-com","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"justonecookbook.com","note":"Namiko Chen's long-running blog and videos on Japanese home cooking.","url":"https://justonecookbook.com","suggested":true},{"name":"RecipeTin Japan","ref":"site/japan-recipetineats-com","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"japan.recipetineats.com","note":"Japanese home recipes from Yumiko, a Japan-born cook, sister site to RecipeTin Eats.","url":"https://japan.recipetineats.com/","suggested":true}]},{"h":"More from Japanese cuisine","links":[["Benihana","dish/benihana"],["Bincho","dish/bincho"],["Boxer Ramen","dish/boxer-ramen"],["Cagen","dish/cagen"],["Chikuwa","dish/chikuwa"],["Curry bread","dish/curry-bread"],["Donburi","dish/donburi"],["Em (restaurant)","dish/em